      "id": 1,
      "text": "Courtland was originally named Jerusalem and was founded in 1791, growing slowly because of difficult transportation.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.courtlandvirginia.com/deptdtl_Dept-20.html",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1888 the Atlantic and Danville Railroad ran through Courtland, sparking the town’s fastest growth spurt.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.courtlandvirginia.com/deptdtl_Dept-20.html",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Courtland hosts the Southampton Agriculture & Forestry Museum, where the historic Vaughn House was moved in 2004 to honor Nat Turner's rebellion.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
